WEBVTT

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:34.940
Hey, do you know?

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:35.830
What?

00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:40.390
Those things crying noisily outside,
they're all cherry boys.

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:41.470
Seriously?!

00:00:41.470 --> 00:00:44.750
Nah, it can't be all.
There are females too.

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:47.630
Nope, only males cry.

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:48.800
Heh...

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:53.740
By crying 'min min'... In human language,
it means "I want to have sex!"

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:54.510
Woah....

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:58.520
They usually just laze around beneath the
ground but just by crying out a little,

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:01.660
they think that they're able to have sex.

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:04.040
Huh?! Isn't that unfair?

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:07.460
I'm getting pissed too.

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:13.460
Ahh... I want to kick up a fuss
this summer and graduate too.

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:17.540
Hey guys, do you realize that your stupidity
level is accelerating in the heat?

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:22.890
But why do we have to come to school at
the end of the first semester?!

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:23.950
Isn't this stupid?

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:26.690
It's because you're stupid, you idiot!

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:30.430
Come to think of it, where's Mafuyu?

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:34.660
He doesn't have remedial class today.

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:36.060
Huh?! Why?!

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:38.570
It's because he scored above 70 points, idiot.

00:01:39.190 --> 00:01:42.590
Say, I don't see you guys together lately.

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:50.910
That's because... he's cooped up at
a senior band member's house.

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:53.200
Hmm... and why all of a sudden?

00:01:54.560 --> 00:02:01.010
<i>Mafuyu is currently stuck to Kaji-san who has the widest range of knowledge about music,</i>

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:05.970
<i>absorbing it like pouring water
into a dried-out pool.</i>

00:02:17.290 --> 00:02:19.920
Ritsuka, you have bad manners!

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:21.500
Put down your phone.

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:23.280
<i>Read and ignore?</i>

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:27.820
<i>What's going on lately?</i>

00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:29.580
Are you listening?

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:32.740
Huh?

00:02:33.490 --> 00:02:34.480
You...

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:36.770
Why are you here?

00:02:37.130 --> 00:02:38.250
I have remedial class today.

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:40.310
Oh.

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:45.380
The details of this dilemma can
be found in the next paragraph.

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:49.360
Within the protaganist, the two
different elements and...

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:53.090
...thoughts are written in detail besides the conversation.

00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:54.760
Let's pick up the important parts.

00:02:58.150 --> 00:02:59.220
Uenoyama-kun...

00:02:59.990 --> 00:03:01.540
Can I go home with you?

00:03:04.690 --> 00:03:06.060
What did you do yesterday?

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:06.590
Eh?

00:03:06.590 --> 00:03:08.590
Because you did not reply my message.

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:14.170
I know it was not on purpose but...

00:03:15.190 --> 00:03:18.700
Yesterday... I was at Kaji-san's
place, writing songs...

00:03:19.610 --> 00:03:21.730
My phone ran out of battery.

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:25.560
Um...

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:28.320
Are you angry?

00:03:30.590 --> 00:03:35.290
You... You're really sticking
to Kaji-san lately.

00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:36.170
That's...

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:40.900
You really think I
would not be angry?

00:03:45.510 --> 00:03:47.760
Damn it. It's nothing.

00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:54.510
W-Why are you angry?

00:03:54.510 --> 00:03:56.790
Huh?! Don't you get it?!

00:03:56.790 --> 00:03:58.730
I d-don't get it.

00:03:59.350 --> 00:04:01.500
Are you stupid?!

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:03.320
Can't you tell from the
current conversation?!

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:05.320
I might understand it...

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:06.170
Which is it?!

00:04:06.440 --> 00:04:08.960
But, if I don't confirm it properly...

00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:15.530
...it might turn out wrong again.

00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:19.030
<i>I'm...</i>

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:23.340
<i>...so lame!!</i>

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:27.350
What time does club
activities start again?

00:04:27.350 --> 00:04:28.510
2 o'clock.

00:04:28.510 --> 00:04:30.260
Then, let's go to the canteen.

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:38.820
Reply my messages properly.

00:04:40.190 --> 00:04:42.510
And let me join in too
when you write songs.

00:04:42.850 --> 00:04:45.060
It's still in progress.

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:46.370
It's fine.

00:04:46.890 --> 00:04:50.230
Kaji-san is not interested in me.

00:04:50.230 --> 00:04:52.540
I know that!

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:05.260
We're in the classroom.

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:08.990
Give me a break.

00:05:08.990 --> 00:05:10.620
There are people at the corridor...

00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:12.430
Yeah, there is...

00:05:19.930 --> 00:05:22.440
<i>Ah, geez...</i>

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:28.910
I can't write the lyrics.

00:05:28.910 --> 00:05:30.860
You're saying it again!

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:34.440
Be careful that I don't
break your index finger.

00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:37.700
Are you alright taking it so leisurely?

00:05:37.700 --> 00:05:39.730
There's a live screening in autumn.

00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:42.290
How's your preparation?

00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:44.200
Who do you think you're talking to?

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:47.570
Hiiragi, how do you write lyrics?

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:49.690
Frankly, by sound.

00:05:49.690 --> 00:05:50.730
Sound?

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:52.590
Ah!

00:05:52.890 --> 00:05:53.770
Oh?

00:05:54.990 --> 00:05:56.740
That's your new boyfriend?

00:05:57.140 --> 00:05:58.630
You've seen him before.

00:05:58.630 --> 00:06:00.590
He looks rather stuck up.

00:06:01.270 --> 00:06:02.240
What's good about him?

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:05.450
He's not as stuck up
as you, so it's fine.

00:06:05.450 --> 00:06:06.180
What?!

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:09.600
Thanks for lending me the yukata.

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:11.780
Hurry up and get together
with Shizu-chan.

00:06:12.270 --> 00:06:13.930
Huh?!! How-

00:06:23.720 --> 00:06:25.380
Shizu's late...

00:06:26.750 --> 00:06:28.850
The fireworks are starting.

00:06:28.850 --> 00:06:30.050
Yeah.

00:06:30.810 --> 00:06:33.400
<i>I didn't think he'd come in a yukata!</i>

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:36.150
How's the yukata?

00:06:36.150 --> 00:06:39.370
Something feels out of place...
But it's fine I guess.

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:40.480
Oh really?

00:06:46.510 --> 00:06:50.050
Meeting outside of the studio
and school is rather refreshing.

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:51.500
You're right.

00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:55.750
I was always either part-timing or at the
studio. We haven't really talk for...

00:06:58.750 --> 00:07:01.960
We did talk.
We even fought once.

00:07:07.750 --> 00:07:10.910
Haruki-san, you've improved recently.

00:07:11.290 --> 00:07:12.530
Eh, really?

00:07:12.880 --> 00:07:16.140
It felt like you really listen
to my part, it helps a lot.

00:07:16.490 --> 00:07:17.540
Thank you so much!

00:07:18.360 --> 00:07:21.070
The drums compliments with the music too.

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:26.590
You need to work a little harder
to improve your level.

00:07:27.310 --> 00:07:27.960
Tsk.

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:29.560
Did you just clicked your tongue at me?!

00:07:30.310 --> 00:07:31.550
Well then, I'm leaving.

00:07:32.200 --> 00:07:33.230
Good job!

00:07:33.230 --> 00:07:34.760
Thanks for the hard work.

00:07:41.910 --> 00:07:45.340
Hey, are you really coming
to my house now?

00:07:45.970 --> 00:07:47.510
<i>Actually, today...</i>

00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:51.100
<i>Mafuyu is coming for a stayover!</i>

00:07:52.260 --> 00:07:55.320
<i>The reason is because today's practice ended late and</i>

00:07:55.320 --> 00:07:58.240
<i>tomorrow's school re-opening ceremony starts early.</i>

00:07:58.240 --> 00:08:02.250
<i>It's just so that it's nearer going to school.</i>

00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:05.410
<i>I have nothing to be ashamed of! Probably...</i>

00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:07.510
<i>But is it really okay?</i>

00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:08.660
<i>Is it alright?</i>

00:08:08.980 --> 00:08:10.110
<i>Actually, what is?</i>

00:08:10.850 --> 00:08:12.880
<i>My family is there, so it's fine.</i>

00:08:17.170 --> 00:08:21.160
Cicadas are actually crying out
"I want to have sex!"

00:08:25.550 --> 00:08:26.410
SHUT UP!

00:08:45.600 --> 00:08:46.510
I'm done.

00:08:47.230 --> 00:08:48.440
Oh...!

00:08:51.460 --> 00:08:54.650
When you think about it,
it sure is a sudden change of plans.

00:08:54.650 --> 00:08:59.880
<i>It's gonna be okay, my brother's
next door. It's fine!</i>

00:09:00.880 --> 00:09:03.640
Let's just go to sleep, pronto.

00:09:03.890 --> 00:09:05.080
Pronto?

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:08.790
Good night.

00:09:13.660 --> 00:09:14.580
Good night.

00:09:25.740 --> 00:09:28.450
<i>Yeah right, how can I sleep right away?!</i>

00:09:28.450 --> 00:09:31.930
<i>I shouldn't have gone with the flow
and invited him over to stay.</i>

00:09:37.430 --> 00:09:47.000
<i>In the first place, it's not like I've never thought about how I feel, or what I want to do with a guy.</i>

00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:50.320
<i>I've thought about it but...</i>

00:09:53.140 --> 00:09:54.290
That clock...

00:09:57.150 --> 00:09:59.260
It's the same clock at Yuki's place.

00:10:09.660 --> 00:10:10.520
You...

00:10:11.700 --> 00:10:12.520
I'm sorry...

00:10:13.220 --> 00:10:15.720
Did I... say something weird?

00:10:15.720 --> 00:10:18.090
No! It's not that!

00:10:19.700 --> 00:10:27.660
I don't really know about your past, but don't look like you're gonna cry alone when I'm here.

00:10:44.860 --> 00:10:46.260
I've sent you the recording.

00:10:46.260 --> 00:10:47.150
Thanks.

00:10:47.680 --> 00:10:49.360
Mafuyu, what's with that part?

00:10:49.360 --> 00:10:50.020
Eh?

00:10:50.020 --> 00:10:54.830
Those random phrases slit
in between the "la la la".

00:10:55.320 --> 00:10:56.930
Are you doing trial and error?

00:10:56.930 --> 00:10:58.030
Yeah.

00:11:00.410 --> 00:11:04.040
About the live judging stage,
what's your plan?

00:11:04.040 --> 00:11:08.410
If he can't complete this current song, we'll perform the previous song.

00:11:09.120 --> 00:11:12.780
But if possible, I want to go
with this current song.

00:11:13.070 --> 00:11:13.980
Why?

00:11:13.980 --> 00:11:19.370
Some of the judges have already heard the previous song on the net.

00:11:19.370 --> 00:11:23.560
But that's also why there's a sense of safety performing the old song.

00:11:23.560 --> 00:11:28.090
That's true too... But there's no new impact.

00:11:28.090 --> 00:11:31.410
I want everyone to see Mafuyu's possibilities.

00:11:31.870 --> 00:11:34.070
I think we can still go further.

00:11:35.700 --> 00:11:37.580
Since we've come so far,
I wanna go for it.

00:11:40.740 --> 00:11:42.530
Woah, so cool!

00:11:43.160 --> 00:11:44.830
Woah, so cool!

00:11:47.720 --> 00:11:49.360
Woah, so cool!

00:11:49.360 --> 00:11:49.960
Annoying!

00:11:50.230 --> 00:11:51.880
Anyway, the lyrics!

00:11:54.090 --> 00:11:56.250
<i>Or so I said...</i>

00:11:56.280 --> 00:11:59.290
Let's play ba-ba-basketball!~

00:12:00.580 --> 00:12:02.250
Uenoyama, let's go!

00:12:05.180 --> 00:12:08.030
I think we need a different approach.

00:12:08.030 --> 00:12:08.780
Huh?

00:12:08.780 --> 00:12:10.520
To the lyrics.

00:12:11.010 --> 00:12:14.530
You said you wanted to write
a different kind of song.

00:12:16.220 --> 00:12:20.220
It's not like I don't have
any ideas at all.

00:12:20.220 --> 00:12:26.770
But when I feel like I've almost got it,
I keep feeling there's a piece missing.

00:12:27.720 --> 00:12:30.070
Then, why don't you go look for it?

00:12:31.350 --> 00:12:34.910
You're the type that gets inspiration
from your own feelings...

00:12:34.910 --> 00:12:38.530
...or things that are happening
with people around you.

00:12:43.890 --> 00:12:46.760
Thank you for the food!

00:12:47.990 --> 00:12:51.480
Finally, there are some cooling days.

00:12:51.480 --> 00:12:53.730
Club activities during summer was hell.

00:12:53.730 --> 00:12:56.850
It's because our school's
gym facilities sucks.

00:12:56.850 --> 00:12:59.840
Do you have band practice everyday like club activities?

00:13:00.560 --> 00:13:02.620
Mostly when we were off school.

00:13:02.620 --> 00:13:04.640
Woah, it's just like club activities.

00:13:04.640 --> 00:13:07.740
You've said that something like
a competition is coming up?

00:13:07.740 --> 00:13:08.320
Yeah.

00:13:08.740 --> 00:13:09.920
When is it?

00:13:11.060 --> 00:13:12.950
Next month.

00:13:16.870 --> 00:13:17.600
Mafuyu.

00:13:19.630 --> 00:13:21.810
The judging day has been announced.

00:13:22.410 --> 00:13:23.450
You think you can make it?

00:13:23.450 --> 00:13:24.740
Yeah.

00:13:24.740 --> 00:13:26.250
If it's the lyrics, it's done.

00:13:27.230 --> 00:13:28.600
We can go for it.

00:13:38.100 --> 00:13:40.590
Hey... Mafuyu?

00:13:41.360 --> 00:13:42.460
What is it?

00:13:46.550 --> 00:13:49.520
I want you to listen to it first.

00:13:50.800 --> 00:13:51.640
Here?

00:13:52.050 --> 00:13:52.740
Yeah.

00:13:55.280 --> 00:13:59.740
<i>Fingers will become apart...</i>

00:14:01.170 --> 00:14:05.290
<i>No matter how much you wish for it...</i>

00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:16.890
♪ Even if I can't sleep, dawn will break

00:14:16.890 --> 00:14:23.380
♪ As I gaze over it

00:14:23.380 --> 00:14:29.480
♪ Things are changing, things are ending

00:14:29.480 --> 00:14:34.270
♪ Things are beginning

00:14:35.530 --> 00:14:36.720
<i>Even so...</i>

00:14:37.410 --> 00:14:44.200
♪ Even if you're not here, dawn will break

00:14:44.200 --> 00:14:50.480
♪ Our separated hands will one day reconnect

00:14:51.200 --> 00:15:02.410
♪ At the end of the long night, one will realize there's light

00:15:03.210 --> 00:15:09.730
♪ That's why even if it's scary, I can keep on living

00:15:09.730 --> 00:15:15.500
♪ When the sun rises, I'll start walking again

00:15:16.110 --> 00:15:22.030
♪ Look, dawn is breaking soon

00:15:22.450 --> 00:15:25.610
♪ That's why, it'll be okay

00:15:42.470 --> 00:15:43.610
Uenoyama-kun?

00:15:47.440 --> 00:15:49.070
<i>Ah, damn it...</i>

00:15:50.300 --> 00:15:52.290
<i>When you sing such a song...</i>

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:54.720
I think it's good.

00:15:55.560 --> 00:15:57.790
<i>Dissatisfaction, uneasiness...</i>

00:15:57.790 --> 00:15:59.660
<i>All of them don't matter.</i>

00:16:03.670 --> 00:16:06.350
<i>He made it all frivolous.</i>

00:16:10.990 --> 00:16:11.970
Mafuyu!

00:16:13.110 --> 00:16:13.990
Hiiragi.

00:16:14.640 --> 00:16:19.920
Uenoyama-kun, these are my childhood
friends... Shizusumi, Hiiragi.

00:16:19.920 --> 00:16:22.120
They're both performing today.

00:16:22.120 --> 00:16:24.320
Ohh... Hello.

00:16:24.320 --> 00:16:27.910
I've mentioned about him
before... Uenoyama-kun...

00:16:28.440 --> 00:16:29.290
My boyfriend.

00:16:30.220 --> 00:16:30.860
Eh?!

00:16:31.460 --> 00:16:33.610
He plays the guitar for our band.

00:16:35.290 --> 00:16:37.630
Ohh...?

00:16:39.350 --> 00:16:40.760
Boyfriend?

00:16:40.760 --> 00:16:43.670
It's your first time meeting
him right, Shizu-chan?

00:16:43.670 --> 00:16:44.330
Er..

00:16:44.330 --> 00:16:46.270
You've met Hiiragi before, right?

00:16:49.350 --> 00:16:50.780
You don't remember?

00:16:52.630 --> 00:16:54.240
How nasty!

00:16:54.980 --> 00:16:57.650
Why are you even here today?

00:16:57.650 --> 00:16:59.580
Your band is performing tomorrow, right?

00:17:00.500 --> 00:17:04.070
In the end, you're just high schoolers.
Enjoying it as a part of the crowd?

00:17:06.940 --> 00:17:08.080
<i>I get it.</i>

00:17:08.770 --> 00:17:12.440
But it sure looks like a regular live.

00:17:12.440 --> 00:17:13.830
How are they judging it?

00:17:14.530 --> 00:17:16.500
We received a paper
when you enter, right?!

00:17:16.500 --> 00:17:19.330
You're supposed to vote here and they'll count the results.

00:17:19.330 --> 00:17:20.720
Oh...

00:17:20.720 --> 00:17:23.420
<i>There's something wrong with all
of you having the same reaction.</i>

00:17:24.180 --> 00:17:28.270
Well then, we've gotta meet up
with the other members.

00:17:28.270 --> 00:17:31.820
Okay, let me know how's the
sound from the back later.

00:17:31.820 --> 00:17:32.790
Sure.

00:17:33.260 --> 00:17:34.210
Good luck.

00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:36.430
Watch closely!

00:17:37.960 --> 00:17:41.110
I wonder where does all that
confidence come from...

00:17:44.420 --> 00:17:46.420
That was amazing.

00:17:46.420 --> 00:17:50.600
Yeah, it was.
They were all really good.

00:17:50.600 --> 00:17:52.520
Hiiragi was great too.

00:17:52.520 --> 00:17:55.020
I don't want to admit it
but he's really good.

00:17:55.020 --> 00:17:59.080
He has the talent of a record producer.
He's on a different level.

00:17:59.610 --> 00:18:01.300
Those guys that went next too...

00:18:01.900 --> 00:18:02.940
What?

00:18:03.650 --> 00:18:05.520
W-What is it?!

00:18:08.810 --> 00:18:11.650
What should I do?
I'm starting to get nervous.

00:18:11.650 --> 00:18:14.230
What?! You actually get nervous?

00:18:14.830 --> 00:18:19.140
I'm starting to wonder if I'll be able to
sing it properly or not... and I get scared.

00:18:20.840 --> 00:18:23.550
I want to get these feelings across.
I want them to understand.

00:18:24.310 --> 00:18:25.710
I think I'm getting a little greedy.

00:18:27.510 --> 00:18:29.180
You've changed...

00:18:30.310 --> 00:18:32.830
At first, you were like, "I can't join a band."

00:18:32.830 --> 00:18:36.890
"I'm not thinking about anything.
I can't express myself."

00:18:36.890 --> 00:18:37.920
You were so hesitant.

00:18:41.850 --> 00:18:42.560
Come here.

00:18:45.470 --> 00:18:46.420
Don't worry.

00:18:47.560 --> 00:18:49.490
You're way cooler than anyone else.

00:18:50.130 --> 00:18:50.930
Yes.

00:18:51.240 --> 00:18:52.580
Why so formal all of a sudden?

00:18:57.560 --> 00:18:59.440
Everyone, thank you for waiting!

00:18:59.440 --> 00:19:03.800
Announcing the results for the
Countdown-Fes Amateur Contest.

00:19:03.800 --> 00:19:05.750
The winner is...

00:19:06.930 --> 00:19:08.250
SYH!

